    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q44",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$5^x=13-5^{x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_5\\left(\\frac12\\right)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5^x+25\\cdot5^x&=13\\\\26\\cdot5^x&=13\\\\5^x&=\\frac12\\\\x&=\\log_5\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q45",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$4^x=15-4^{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_4 3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4^x+4\\cdot4^x&=15\\\\5\\cdot4^x&=15\\\\4^x&=3\\\\x&=\\log_4 3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q46",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3^{x+1}-3^x=8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_3 4$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3\\cdot3^x-3^x&=8\\\\2\\cdot3^x&=8\\\\3^x&=4\\\\x&=\\log_3 4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q47",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$8^x=2-2^{3x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\ln(\\frac{2}{3})}{3\\ln2}$\n\nWrite both exponential terms in base 2, then collect them and take logarithms.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2^{3x}+2\\cdot2^{3x}&=2\\\\3\\cdot2^{3x}&=2\\\\2^{3x}&=\\frac23\\\\3x\\ln2&=\\ln\\left(\\frac23\\right)\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln(2/3)}{3\\ln2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q48",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$4^x=9^{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\ln3}{\\ln(\\frac{2}{3})}$\n\nTake logarithms of both sides and collect the terms containing $x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x\\ln4&=(x+1)\\ln9\\\\x(\\ln4-\\ln9)&=\\ln9\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln9}{\\ln4-\\ln9}\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln3}{\\ln(2/3)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q49",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$2^x5^{x-1}=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_{10}20$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2^x5^x}{5}&=4\\\\10^x&=20\\\\x&=\\log_{10}20\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q50",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$2^x3^{2x-1}=54$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\ln2+4\\ln3}{\\ln2+2\\ln3}$\n\nUse the product and power laws of logarithms, then collect the terms containing $x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x\\ln2+(2x-1)\\ln3&=\\ln54\\\\x(\\ln2+2\\ln3)&=\\ln54+\\ln3\\\\x(\\ln2+2\\ln3)&=\\ln2+4\\ln3\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln2+4\\ln3}{\\ln2+2\\ln3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q51",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$2^{2x}=5^{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac{\\ln5}{\\ln(\\frac{5}{4})}$\n\nTake logarithms of both sides and collect the terms containing $x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2x\\ln2&=(x-1)\\ln5\\\\x(\\ln5-2\\ln2)&=\\ln5\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln5}{\\ln(5/4)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
